00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.350 align:start position:0%
seventeen-year-old malala yousafzai is  the youngest person to ever win a nobel  prize  she is also the first pakistani to win  the peace award  she shares this year's prize with fellow  children's rights activist kailash  satyati  those attending applauded the two  recipients for their selfless work  the prize committee commended malala for  her clear vision and tireless courage  malala yosef sai's vision was clear  right from the start  girls have a self-evident right to  education  her courage  is almost  indescribable  malala grew up in northern pakistan  since an early age she spoke out in  support of girls rights and against the  extremist ideology of local taliban  groups but her advocacy nearly cost her  her life  in 2012 a taliban soldier boarded her  school bus and then shot her three times  in the head  malala barely survived  her heroic survival made international  headlines she has used her story to  bring attention to her cause  it is for those  forgotten children  who want education  it is for those  frightened children  who want peace  it is for those  voiceless children  who want change  this year's prize is being split between  a hindu man and muslim woman from two  very different backgrounds but both  satyathi and yusuf sai share the same  dream to live in a world where all  children are free
 

